BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (rejected delivery; reconcile acknowledgment before sending another billable post. Respect bid expiration, reserve) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (capacity only as the contract allows, and prevent stale responses from winning after the caller disconnects. Track ping) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (latency, post acknowledgment latency, abandoned calls, buyer answer delay, and multiple winning commitments) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (independently. Start with an illustrative 800-millisecond routing budget where contracts and observed infrastructure) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (support it, rather than asserting a universal vendor service level. Alert when the 95th-percentile ping latency exceeds) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (the configured route budget for five minutes; open the circuit after repeated transport failures and use a contracted) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (alternate with available capacity. If no eligible buyer remains, end or redirect the journey honestly instead of repeatedly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (auctioning an abandoned call. Authenticate incoming disposition callbacks, validate timestamps, and reject duplicate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (event identifiers. A forged paid-conversion callback can inflate ad bidding even if it never changes the accounting) Tj ET
